* **Lab:** 02

## Objective

To develop a Book Management API using Node.js, Express.js and SQLite, implementing CRUD operations to manage book records.

## Technologies Used

* Node.js
* Express.js
* SQLite
* JavaScript
* Postman
* VS Code

## Database Structure

Database Name: `books.db`

Table Name: `book`

| Column | Data Type           |
| ------ | ------------------- |
| id     | INTEGER PRIMARY KEY |
| title  | TEXT                |
| author | TEXT                |
| price  | INTEGER             |
| pages  | INTEGER             |

## API Endpoints

| HTTP Method | Endpoint        | Description              |
| ----------- | --------------- | ------------------------ |
| GET         | /books/         | Retrieve all books       |
| GET         | /books/:bookId/ | Retrieve a specific book |
| POST        | /books/         | Add a new book           |
| PUT         | /books/:bookId/ | Update book details      |
| DELETE      | /books/:bookId/ | Delete a book            |

## CRUD Operations

1. Create: Adds new book records.
2. Read: Retrieves all books or a specific book.
3. Update: Modifies existing book details.
4. Delete: Removes a book from the database.

## Screenshots

Postman screenshots demonstrating all CRUD operations are available in the `screenshots` folder.

## How to Run

1. Install dependencies:

   `npm install`

2. Start the application:

   `npm run dev`

3. Open Postman and test the API endpoints using:

   `http://localhost:3000`

## Result

Successfully developed and tested a Book Management API using Node.js, Express.js and SQLite. All five API endpoints were tested using Postman.
